{"slug":"longest-common-subsequence","title":"The Longest Subsequence Two Words Share","topic":"dp","difficulty":"medium","order":741,"tags":["dp","lcs","string","two-strings"],"timeLimitMs":2000,"concept":{"title":"A table over the prefixes of both words: match the last letters or drop one of them","body":["Two words are given. A *subsequence* of a word is obtained by deleting some letters (possibly none) and keeping the order of the rest. Find the length of the **longest common subsequence** (LCS) of the two words. For `abcde` and `ace` it is 3 (`ace`). (This is different from the common *substring* problem, where the letters must be next to each other.)","Let `lcs(i, j)` be the length of the LCS of the first `i` letters of `a` and the first `j` letters of `b`; if one prefix is empty it is 0. Look at the last letters `a[i]` and `b[j]`. If they are **equal**, there is an optimal solution that uses both of them together: `lcs(i, j) = lcs(i - 1, j - 1) + 1`. If they differ, at least one of them is not used, so **`lcs(i, j) = max(lcs(i - 1, j), lcs(i, j - 1))`**.",{"code":"prev = [0] * (len(b) + 1)\nfor ch in a:\n    cur = [0] * (len(b) + 1)\n    for j in range(len(b)):\n        if b[j] == ch:\n            cur[j + 1] = prev[j] + 1\n        else:\n            cur[j + 1] = max(cur[j], prev[j + 1])\n    prev = cur\nprint(prev[len(b)])"},"The table has `|a| * |b|` cells; each cell looks at three neighbours, and a row needs only the row above it, so two rows are enough: O(|a| * |b|) time, O(|b|) memory. The LCS table is the basis of many tools that compare texts (it is what a diff program uses to show what changed)."]},"statement":["Two words `a` and `b` are given. Print the length of their longest common subsequence: the longest word that can be obtained from both by deleting some letters (keeping the order of the remaining ones)."],"inputFormat":["The first line has the string `a`.","The second line has the string `b`."],"outputFormat":["Print the length of the longest common subsequence."],"constraints":["1 <= length of a, length of b <= 1200","Both strings consist of lowercase English letters."],"examples":[{"input":"abcde\nace\n","output":"3\n","note":"The common subsequence ace: 3."},{"input":"abc\ndef\n","output":"0\n","note":"No common letter: 0."}],"hints":["Let lcs(i, j) be the answer for the first i letters of a and the first j letters of b.","If the last letters are equal, add 1 to lcs(i - 1, j - 1); otherwise take the larger of lcs(i - 1, j) and lcs(i, j - 1).","Two rows of the table are enough."],"starter":{"python":"import sys\ninput = sys.stdin.readline\n\na = input().strip()\nb = input().strip()\n\n# Your code here\n","cpp":"#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <string>\nusing namespace std;\n\nint main() {\n    ios::sync_with_stdio(false);\n    cin.tie(nullptr);\n\n    string a;\n    cin >> a;\n    string b;\n    cin >> b;\n\n    // Your code here\n\n    return 0;\n}\n","java":"import java.io.*;\nimport java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    static BufferedReader in = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(System.in));\n    static StringTokenizer tokens = new StringTokenizer(\"\");\n\n    static String next() throws IOException {\n        while (!tokens.hasMoreTokens()) {\n            tokens = new StringTokenizer(in.readLine());\n        }\n        return tokens.nextToken();\n    }\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) throws IOException {\n        String a = next();\n        String b = next();\n\n        // Your code here\n    }\n}\n"},"solution":{"explanation":["lcs(i, j) = lcs(i - 1, j - 1) + 1 when the letters a[i] and b[j] are equal and max(lcs(i - 1, j), lcs(i, j - 1)) otherwise, computed row by row with two rows."],"complexity":"Time O(|a| * |b|), space O(|b|).","code":{"python":"import sys\ninput = sys.stdin.readline\n\na = input().strip()\nb = input().strip()\n\nprev = [0] * (len(b) + 1)\nfor ch in a:\n    cur = [0] * (len(b) + 1)\n    for j in range(len(b)):\n        if b[j] == ch:\n            cur[j + 1] = prev[j] + 1\n        else:\n            cur[j + 1] = cur[j] if cur[j] > prev[j + 1] else prev[j + 1]\n    prev = cur\nprint(prev[len(b)])\n","cpp":"#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <string>\nusing namespace std;\n\nint main() {\n    ios::sync_with_stdio(false);\n    cin.tie(nullptr);\n\n    string a;\n    cin >> a;\n    string b;\n    cin >> b;\n\n    int n = (int)a.size(), m = (int)b.size();\n    vector<int> prev(m + 1, 0), cur(m + 1, 0);\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n        for (int j = 0; j < m; j++) {\n            if (a[i] == b[j]) cur[j + 1] = prev[j] + 1;\n            else cur[j + 1] = max(cur[j], prev[j + 1]);\n        }\n        swap(prev, cur);\n    }\n    cout << prev[m] << \"\\n\";\n\n    return 0;\n}\n","java":"import java.io.*;\nimport java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    static BufferedReader in = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(System.in));\n    static StringTokenizer tokens = new StringTokenizer(\"\");\n\n    static String next() throws IOException {\n        while (!tokens.hasMoreTokens()) {\n            tokens = new StringTokenizer(in.readLine());\n        }\n        return tokens.nextToken();\n    }\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) throws IOException {\n        String a = next();\n        String b = next();\n\n        int n = a.length(), m = b.length();\n        int[] prev = new int[m + 1];\n        int[] cur = new int[m + 1];\n        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n            for (int j = 0; j < m; j++) {\n                if (a.charAt(i) == b.charAt(j)) cur[j + 1] = prev[j] + 1;\n                else cur[j + 1] = Math.max(cur[j], prev[j + 1]);\n            }\n            int[] swap = prev;\n            prev = cur;\n            cur = swap;\n        }\n        System.out.println(prev[m]);\n    }\n}\n"}},"tests":[{"input":"abcde\nace\n","output":"3\n"},{"input":"abc\ndef\n","output":"0\n"},{"input":"a\na\n","output":"1\n"},{"input":"a\nb\n","output":"0\n"},{"input":"abc\nabc\n","output":"3\n"},{"input":"baaabbabbbbbaaaaabba\nbaaabaabbbabaaabaaaaaaaba\n","output":"18\n"},{"input":"cccacbbaacccbbabbcaccacbacabbccbccaacaaaccbaacacacbaccbbbaacbccccabbaccbacabccacbabbcaacacaaacbbbbbc\nabcbcacaacacbaabcccaacbacbbbbababccacacabcabcaacbacccbccbacbcbabaccbbcbcabcbbbcccaabacababbbcabcabcc\n","output":"72\n"},{"input":"\\n","output":"222\n"},{"input":"\\n","output":"651\n"},{"input":"\\n","output":"384\n"},{"input":"\\n","output":"966\n"},{"input":"\\n","output":"850\n"},{"input":"b\\n","output":"1\n"},{"input":"\nb\n","output":"1\n"},{"input":"\\n","output":"900\n"},{"input":"\\n","output":"1200\n"},{"input":"\\n","output":"1200\n"},{"input":"\\n","output":"0\n"},{"input":"\\n","output":"1199\n"},{"input":"\\n","output":"608\n"}]}